      "worked_solution": "The length of the semi-minor axis is half the length of the minor axis.\n\n- The minor axis is the shortest diameter of the ellipse, which is the line segment bounded by the points $(-1,-3)$ and $(7,-3).$ So, the length of the minor axis is $7-(-1)=8.$\n\n- The length of the semi-minor axis, then, is $\\frac{8}{2}=4.$",
